    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced><mo>  </mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>IV</mi></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>iv</mi></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfenced><mo>⇒</mo></math> incorrect, because, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></mrow></msub></math> has no nodal plane.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo> </mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>II</mi></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>ii</mi></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mfenced><mo>⇒</mo></math> correct, because <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo> </mo></math>orbital has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo></math>radial node.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/33_solu_chem_pa1.jpg\"/></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mfenced><mo>  </mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>III</mi></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>iii</mi></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mfenced><mo>⇒</mo></math> incorrect, because probability density for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo> </mo></math>at nucleus is zero.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo> </mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>ii</mi></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mfenced><mo>⇒</mo></math> incorrect, because <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo> </mo></math>orbital has no radial node.</p><p> </p>",
